Que. State the behaviour of marginal product in the Law of Variable Proportions.
Explain the causes of this behaviour.
Ans. There are three phases of change in MP:
MP rises: When the variable input is increased, efficient utilisation of the
fixed inputs takes place due to specialisation. This raises efficiency of the
variable input.
MP falls but is positive: Beyond a point, increasing variable input puts
pressure on fixed inputs.
MP continues to fall and is negative: There is so much pressure of the
variable input on the fixed inputs that total product starts declining.
